+The fair-coin null is a calibration model. It is not a claim that actual submissions guess, nor a
+randomization test justified solely by class balance. A deterministic constant predictor under exact
+fixed balance, for example, has a different conditional score distribution. Correlated problem–model
+outcomes, unequal item difficulties or an imperfectly balanced label composition can also invalidate
+the binomial calibration. The analysis should therefore be read as “what this small grid can estab-
+lish under this transparent reference,” rather than as unconditional evidence about the private task
+distribution.
