+The conventional false-discovery-rate guarantee requires valid owner p-values and suitable depen-
+dence conditions, such as independent owners. Public methods can share code, data, observations
+and leaderboard feedback. We do not observe those dependencies. Bonferroni avoids the across-
+owner dependence requirement when its input p-values are valid, but still inherits the binomial item
+model and the independent-submission adjustment. Equal counts under the two corrections are use-
+ful sensitivity evidence within this model; they do not remove its assumptions.
