+A group is concordant when all included binary labels agree. The reference count sums the proba-
+bilities of all-positive or all-negative labels at each observed group size under independent Bernoulli
+draws at pooled prevalence. It is descriptive, not a significance test. The no-gap sensitivity labels
+every training row by the lower public threshold, then collapses the larger checkpoint’s effort vari-
+ants by the minimum binary label. Both the cohort and collapse rule change. The sample proxy
+uses the public threshold band and is not a private competition label. These distinctions prevent a
+label-concordance table from being read as evidence about unseen private outcomes.
